  "scope": "states",
  "table": {
   "report": "709",
   "handbook": 79,
   "title": "Pattern of receipts of the state governments"
  },
  "latestPeriod": "2025-26 (financial year)",
  "coverage": "Where the states' money comes from: their own taxes, their share of central taxes, grants from the Centre, capital receipts, ₹ crore, 1970-71 on",
  "note": "RBI, Pattern of receipts of the state governments (DBIE report 709; Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy). Amounts in ₹ crore (DBIE serves rupees). 'Sales tax' is the states' sales tax and VAT, and from 2017-18 their GST as the RBI groups it. Capital receipts include the public account on a net basis (Handbook note 5). Stages, from the printed table's own note: accounts to 2023-24, the revised estimate for 2024-25 and the budget estimate for 2025-26, each in its own series (suffix __re and __be), never one line. Cross-checked against the printed table (Innovation Hub export of Handbook report 79): 636 of 636 figures match."
 },
